{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can use client-side tests to test code that internally uses the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The idea is to declare expected requests and to provide “stub” responses so that you can focus on testing the code in isolation (that is, without running a server). The following example shows how to do so:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();\n\nMockRestServiceServer mockServer = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).build();\nmockServer.expect(requestTo(\"/greeting\")).andRespond(withSuccess());\n\n// Test code that uses the above RestTemplate ...\n\nmockServer.verify();"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "val restTemplate = RestTemplate()\n\nval mockServer = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).build()\nmockServer.expect(requestTo(\"/greeting\")).andRespond(withSuccess())\n\n// Test code that uses the above RestTemplate ...\n\nmockServer.verify()"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the preceding example, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MockRestServiceServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (the central class for client-side REST tests) configures the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " with a custom "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ClientHttpRequestFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that asserts actual requests against expectations and returns “stub” responses. In this case, we expect a request to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/greeting"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and want to return a 200 response with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "text/plain"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " content. We can define additional expected requests and stub responses as needed. When we define expected requests and stub responses, the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " can be used in client-side code as usual. At the end of testing, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "mockServer.verify()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " can be used to verify that all expectations have been satisfied."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, requests are expected in the order in which expectations were declared. You can set the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ignoreExpectOrder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option when building the server, in which case all expectations are checked (in order) to find a match for a given request. That means requests are allowed to come in any order. The following example uses "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ignoreExpectOrder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "server = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).ignoreExpectOrder(true).build();"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "server = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).ignoreExpectOrder(true).build()"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Even with unordered requests by default, each request is allowed to run once only. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "expect"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method provides an overloaded variant that accepts an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ExpectedCount"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " argument that specifies a count range (for example, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "once"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "manyTimes"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "max"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "min"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "between"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and so on). The following example uses "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "times"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();\n\nMockRestServiceServer mockServer = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).build();\nmockServer.expect(times(2), requestTo(\"/something\")).andRespond(withSuccess());\nmockServer.expect(times(3), requestTo(\"/somewhere\")).andRespond(withSuccess());\n\n// ...\n\nmockServer.verify();"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "val restTemplate = RestTemplate()\n\nval mockServer = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).build()\nmockServer.expect(times(2), requestTo(\"/something\")).andRespond(withSuccess())\nmockServer.expect(times(3), requestTo(\"/somewhere\")).andRespond(withSuccess())\n\n// ...\n\nmockServer.verify()"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that, when "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ignoreExpectOrder"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is not set (the default), and, therefore, requests are expected in order of declaration, then that order applies only to the first of any expected request. For example if \"/something\" is expected two times followed by \"/somewhere\" three times, then there should be a request to \"/something\" before there is a request to \"/somewhere\", but, aside from that subsequent \"/something\" and \"/somewhere\", requests can come at any time."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As an alternative to all of the above, the client-side test support also provides a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ClientHttpRequestFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " implementation that you can configure into a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to bind it to a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MockMvc"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " instance. That allows processing requests using actual server-side logic but without running a server. The following example shows how to do so:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "MockMvc mockMvc = MockMvcBuilders.webAppContextSetup(this.wac).build();\nthis.restTemplate = new RestTemplate(new MockMvcClientHttpRequestFactory(mockMvc));\n\n// Test code that uses the above RestTemplate ..."
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "val mockMvc = MockMvcBuilders.webAppContextSetup(this.wac).build()\nrestTemplate = RestTemplate(MockMvcClientHttpRequestFactory(mockMvc))\n\n// Test code that uses the above RestTemplate ..."
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In some cases it may be necessary to perform an actual call to a remote service instead of mocking the response. The following example shows how to do that through "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ExecutingResponseCreator"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "RestTemplate restTemplate = new RestTemplate();\n\n// Create ExecutingResponseCreator with the original request factory\nExecutingResponseCreator withActualResponse = new ExecutingResponseCreator(restTemplate.getRequestFactory());\n\nMockRestServiceServer mockServer = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).build();\nmockServer.expect(requestTo(\"/profile\")).andRespond(withSuccess());\nmockServer.expect(requestTo(\"/quoteOfTheDay\")).andRespond(withActualResponse);\n\n// Test code that uses the above RestTemplate ...\n\nmockServer.verify();"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "val restTemplate = RestTemplate()\n\n// Create ExecutingResponseCreator with the original request factory\nval withActualResponse = new ExecutingResponseCreator(restTemplate.getRequestFactory())\n\nval mockServer = MockRestServiceServer.bindTo(restTemplate).build()\nmockServer.expect(requestTo(\"/profile\")).andRespond(withSuccess())\nmockServer.expect(requestTo(\"/quoteOfTheDay\")).andRespond(withActualResponse)\n\n// Test code that uses the above RestTemplate ...\n\nmockServer.verify()"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the preceding example, we create the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ExecutingResponseCreator"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ClientHttpRequestFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " from the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "before"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MockRestServiceServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " replaces it with a different one that mocks responses. Then we define expectations with two kinds of responses:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "a stub "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "200"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " response for the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "/profile"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " endpoint (no actual request will be executed)"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "a response obtained through a call to the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "/quoteOfTheDay"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " endpoint"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the second case, the request is executed through the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ClientHttpRequestFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that was captured earlier. This generates a response that could, for example, come from an actual remote server, depending on how the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestTemplate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " was originally configured."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As with server-side tests, the fluent API for client-side tests requires a few static imports. Those are easy to find by searching for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MockRest*"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Eclipse users should add "
